namespace Pscf {
namespace Rp {

/*!
\page rp_HamiltonianAnalyzer_page HamiltonianAnalyzer

This analyzer can output instantaneous values and averages of the total 
field theoretic hamiltonian \f$ H \f$ and its ideal gas and field 
contributions.

\see HamiltonianAnalyzer (class API)
\see Rp::Simulator

\section rp_HamiltonianAnalyzer_definitions_sec Definitions

The ideal and field contributions to the Hamiltonian that are 
computed and analyzed by this class are the quantities denoted by 
\f$ \tilde{H}_{\rm id} \f$ and \f$ \tilde{H}_{\rm f} \f$ that are 
defined \ref psfts_psa_pressure_sec "here".  In a system with no
associated perturbation, Hamiltonian \f$ H \f$ is given by a sum 
\f$ H = \tilde{H}_{\rm id} + \tilde{H}_{\rm f} \f$.

<em> For users who read the source code </em>: 
The quantities \f$ H \f$, \f$ \tilde{H}_{\rm id} \f$ and 
\f$ \tilde{H}_{rm f} \f$ that are analyzed by this class are computed by 
the Rp::Simulator::computeHamiltonian() function and returned by the 
Rp::Simulator::hamiltonian(), Rp::Simulator::idealHamiltonian() and 
Rp::Simulator::fieldHamiltonian() accessor functions, respectively.
 
\section rp_HamiltonianAnalyzer_parameter_sec Parameter file

Parameter file block format:
\code
HamiltonianAnalyzer{
  interval*           int    (1 by default)
  outputFileName      string
  nSamplePerOutput*   int    (1 by default)
}
\endcode
Meanings of the parameters:
<table>
  <tr>
    <td> <b> Label </b>  </td>
    <td> <b> Description </b>  </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td> interval </td>
    <td> number of steps between data samples </td>
  </tr>
    <tr>
     <td> outputFileName </td>
     <td> name of output file </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
     <td>nSamplePerOutput * </td>
     <td>number of samples per block average output to file</td>
  </tr>
</table>


\section rp_HamiltonianAnalyzer_output_sec Output

In the following, "{outputFileName}" is used to represent the string
value of the outputFileName parameter within descriptions of output
file names.

<b> Output during a simulation: </b>:

If nSamplePerOutput > 0, the block averages of the total Hamiltonian
and its components are output to the file {outputFileName}.dat every
interval \* nSamplerPerBlock simulation steps. This file contains four 
columns. The first column contains an integer step counter for the first 
simulation step or trajectory file frame in a block. The next three 
columns contain block averaged values of \f$ \tilde{H}_{\rm id} \f$, 
\f$ \tilde{H}_{\rm f} \f$, and \f$ H \f$, listed in that order.

If nSamplePerOutput == 1 (or if this optional parameter is omitted),
then instantaneous values of \f$ H_{\rm id} \f$, \f$ H_{\rm f} \f$ and 
\f$ H \f$ are output to {outputFileName}.dat every interval time steps, 
with no block averaging.

If nSamplerPerBlock = 0, the {outputFileName}.dat data file is not
created.

If a simulation uses a perturbation, the contribution to the 
Hamiltonian arising from the perturbation is included in all reported
values of \f$ H \f$, but is not analyzed separately or listed as a 
separated column in the {outputFileName}.dat file. If no perturbation 
exists, then \f$ H = \tilde{H}_{\rm id} + \tilde{H}_{\rm f} \f$. 

<b> Final output: </b>:

At the end of the simulation or analysis of a trajectory file:

  - average values for \f$ H_{\rm id} \f$, \f$ H_{\rm f} \f$ and
    \f$ H \f$ along with corresponding error estimates are output 
    to the file {outputFileName}.ave

  - Details of the blocking error analysis for these quantities are 
    output to {outputFileName}.aer

See the discussion of \ref psfts_algo_analyzer_error_sec "error analysis"
for further details. 
*/

}
}
